meta {
  name: Link a board to the project
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

put {
  url: {{bffUrl}}/api/v1/projects/{{projectId}}/task-manager
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "integration_id": "{{integrationId}}",
    "external_space_id": "sp-901",
    "external_project_id": "pj-42",
    "card_types": ["bug", "feature"]
  }
}

docs {
  In the CORE, UpdateProject is a replacement: sending the project without the
  fields you do not want to lose erases them. The edge reads the current project,
  overlays only the link and resends it — which is why here you send only the board,
  and the name, the description and the rules survive.

  `card_types` comes from the provider and is dynamic: the platform imposes no card
  vocabulary (ADR-0009).
}
